---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const faq = [
	{
		question: 'When do I need a fire water cannon instead of standard sprinklers?',
		answer: 'Water cannons suit large open or high-ceiling spaces where sprinkler coverage is impractical: petrochemical process areas, oil and LNG tank farms, loading terminals, aircraft hangars and large warehouses. They deliver a concentrated high-flow jet over 50–110 metres, controlled manually, remotely or automatically.'
	},
	{
		question: 'What flow rate and range do I need?',
		answer: 'Flow follows the hazard: 5–30 L/s suits warehouse and atrium protection, while 30–200 L/s serves tank farms and process units. Range depends on inlet pressure — typically 50–110 m at rated flow. Send your site layout and our engineers will size the model.'
	},
	{
		question: 'Remote-controlled or auto-tracking cannon — which should I choose?',
		answer: 'If an operator can be present, remote-controlled models give flexible manual override at a safe distance. For unmanned or 24/7-risk areas, auto-tracking cannons with IR/UV detection detect, aim and jet within 30 seconds without human intervention.'
	},
	{
		question: 'Can water cannons be used with foam?',
		answer: 'Yes. Our PS series supports both water and foam media, and foam proportioning can be integrated for class B (liquid fuel) hazards. The PSG30 foam cabinet is a complete packaged option for smaller fuel and chemical risks.'
	},
	{
		question: 'Do you supply the cannon with the full system — valves, couplings, pumps?',
		answer: 'Yes. As a fluid equipment manufacturer we supply matched valves, couplings, hydrants and accessories for the complete suppression loop, so your cannon order can be a single-source package.'
	}
];

const cannonProducts = [
	{
		slug: 'auto-tracking-jet-suppression-cannon-zdms',
		name: 'Auto-Tracking Cannon (ZDMS)',
		img: '/assets/06_extinguishing_cannons/cannon_p45.png?v=20260729',
		desc: 'IR/UV detection, 5–150 L/s'
	},
	{
		slug: 'manual-fire-water-cannon-ps',
		name: 'Manual Water Cannon (PS)',
		img: 'https://sc02.alicdn.com/kf/A192331c7a7d948a6927a9221489369dcz.png',
		desc: '20–200 L/s, up to 110 m'
	},
	{
		slug: 'foam-fire-hydrant-cabinet-psg30',
		name: 'Foam Cabinet (PSG30)',
		img: '/assets/06_extinguishing_cannons/cannon_p42.png?v=20260729',
		desc: '3% AFFF for fuel/chemical fires'
	}
];
---

<Layout
	title="Fire Water Cannon Buying Guide: Fixed, Remote or Smart? (2026)"
	description="How to choose a fire water cannon: fixed vs remote vs auto-tracking, sizing flow and range, control modes, foam compatibility and a site-based procurement checklist."
	type="article"
	faq={faq}
	breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Blog', href: '/blog/' }, { name: 'Water Cannon Guide' }]}
>
	<main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 mb-16">
		<!-- Breadcrumbs -->
		<nav class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-6 flex gap-2">
			<a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Home</a>
			<span>/</span>
			<a href="/blog/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Blog</a>
			<span>/</span>
			<span class="text-gray-600">Water Cannon Guide</span>
		</nav>

		<article class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-10">
			<p class="text-brand-red font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-sm mb-3">Industrial Fire Suppression Guide</p>
			<h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 leading-tight tracking-tight">Fire Water Cannon Buying Guide: Fixed, Remote or Smart? (2026)</h1>
			<p class="mt-5 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-lg">A fire water cannon is a high-flow monitor that throws a concentrated jet 50–110 metres — the suppression tool of choice for petrochemical plants, tank farms, terminals and large warehouses where sprinklers cannot reach. The buying decision comes down to four questions: fixed or controllable, what flow, what range, and does it need to think for itself. This guide walks through each.</p>

			<!-- Product strip -->
			<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
				{cannonProducts.map(p => (
					<a href={`/products/${p.slug}/`} class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden hover:border-brand-red hover:shadow-md transition">
						<img src={p.img} alt={p.name} loading="lazy" class="w-full h-28 object-contain bg-white p-2" />
						<div class="p-3">
							<p class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-800 group-hover:text-brand-red leading-snug transition-colors">{p.name}</p>
							<p class="text-[10px] text-gray-400 mt-1 line-clamp-2">{p.desc}</p>
						</div>
					</a>
				))}
			</div>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">1. Do You Actually Need a Water Cannon?</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Water cannons earn their cost in three situations: <strong>large open areas</strong> (warehouses, atriums, hangars) where fixed sprinklers would need impractical densities; <strong>outdoor hazards</strong> (tank farms, loading racks, process units) where there is no ceiling to mount sprinklers; and <strong>high-value risks</strong> where fast, concentrated suppression beats widespread water damage. If your site is an enclosed, standard-occupancy building, a sprinkler system is likely the right answer instead — see our <a href="/fire-sprinkler-systems/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">sprinkler systems page</a>.</p>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">2. Fixed, Remote or Auto-Tracking?</h2>
			<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 my-5">
				<table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-200 text-sm">
					<thead class="bg-gray-50">
						<tr>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">How it operates</th>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Best for</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody class="bg-white divide-y divide-gray-200">
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Fixed monitor</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Manual lever aiming, self-locking gear holds position</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Sites with operators on duty; cost-effective baseline</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Remote-controlled</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Wired/wireless control from safe distance, 360° rotation</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Hazards too close for manual operation</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Auto-tracking</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">IR/UV flame detection, autonomous aim and jet in ~30s</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Unmanned areas, 24/7 risk, fast response requirements</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The <a href="/products/auto-tracking-jet-suppression-cannon-zdms/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZDMS auto-tracking cannon</a> combines infrared and ultraviolet sensing to confirm a real flame before it acts — reducing false triggers — and supports manual override from a PC, mobile app or central cabinet. The <a href="/products/manual-fire-water-cannon-ps/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">PS manual series</a> remains the dependable low-cost workhorse where operators are present.</p>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">3. Sizing Flow and Range</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Two numbers define a cannon's capability: <strong>flow</strong> (L/s) and <strong>jet range</strong> (m). Flow is set by the hazard and the firewater demand calculation; range is set by inlet pressure and nozzle design.</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-4">
				<li><strong>Warehouses &amp; atriums</strong>: 5–30 L/s cannons, monitoring radius 40–65 m — the ZDMS sweet spot.</li>
				<li><strong>Tank farms &amp; process units</strong>: 30–200 L/s with jet ranges to 110 m — the PS series range.</li>
				<li><strong>Foam hazards</strong>: specify foam proportioning or a packaged unit like the <a href="/products/foam-fire-hydrant-cabinet-psg30/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">PSG30 foam cabinet</a> for class B risks.</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Rule of thumb: if you cannot confidently size the flow, send the site layout and firewater demand to the supplier — the correct model follows from the hazard, not from a catalogue page.</p>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">4. Control and Integration</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Auto-tracking cannons are only as useful as their integration: they should link to the fire alarm panel, and the manual override path (local cabinet or remote station) must be tested with your operators. Check the communication interface, the explosion-proof rating if the cannon sits in a classified area (Exde II BT4 Gb is available), and the IP rating for outdoor exposure.</p>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">5. Procurement Checklist</h2>
			<ol class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-4">
				<li>Define the hazard and firewater demand; confirm cannon flow and range with the supplier.</li>
				<li>Choose control mode: fixed, remote or auto-tracking — match to staffing and response time.</li>
				<li>Confirm media compatibility (water only, or foam proportioning).</li>
				<li>Check explosion-proof and IP ratings for the installation environment.</li>
				<li>Request the full-loop package: cannon, valves, couplings, hydrants — one BOM, one supplier.</li>
				<li>Clarify MOQ, lead time, installation support and spare parts in the commercial offer.</li>
			</ol>

			<!-- Cross-link to landing page -->
			<div class="mt-10 bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-black text-gray-900 tracking-tight">Explore Our Fire Water Cannon Range</h2>
				<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Compare fixed, remote and smart models with full specifications on the <a href="/fire-water-cannon/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">fire water cannon page</a>.</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Related guide -->
			<div class="mt-10 bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-black text-gray-900 tracking-tight">Related Guide: Manual vs Auto-Tracking</h2>
				<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Need a head-to-head technical comparison of manual (PS) and auto-tracking (ZDMS) monitors? See the <a href="/guides/fire-water-monitor-selection-guide/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Fire Water Monitor Selection Guide</a>.</p>
			</div>

			<!-- FAQ -->
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-6 tracking-tight">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4">
				{faq.map(item => (
					<details class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 p-5 open:border-brand-red/30">
						<summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-bold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer list-none">
							<span>{item.question}</span>
							<span class="text-brand-blue text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
						</summary>
						<p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-sm">{item.answer}</p>
					</details>
				))}
			</div>

			<!-- CTA -->
			<div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
				<div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-blue to-blue-800 px-6 sm:px-10 py-10 text-center">
					<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">Need a Water Cannon for Your Site?</h2>
					<p class="mt-3 text-blue-100 max-w-xl mx-auto text-sm leading-relaxed">Send us your site layout, required range and flow — our engineers recommend the right model and reply with a full quotation within 12 hours.</p>
					<div class="mt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-center gap-4">
						<a href="/contact/?product=Fire%20Water%20Cannon" class="px-8 py-4 bg-brand-red text-white font-bold rounded-lg hover:opacity-90 transition">Request a Quote</a>
						<a href="https://wa.me/8618684324501?text=Hi%2C%20I%20need%20a%20fire%20water%20cannon" class="px-8 py-4 bg-white text-brand-blue font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-50 transition" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>
